    "probe_text": "I now have the complete picture. `POST /api/owners` is handled by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (the V2 controller only exposes a paged list). Here is the full ordered sequence.\n\n## Before the controller method runs\n\n1. **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`. Caller must hold the `OWNER_ADMIN` role.\n2. **Bean Validation** on the `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto` (`OwnerFieldsDto.java`), i.e. before any code in `addOwner` executes:\n   - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,30)`, `@Pattern` (letters, up to 3 words joined by space/`'`/`-`)\n   - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,30)`, `@Pattern` (same, trailing `.` allowed)\n   - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,80)`\n   - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,20)`\n   - `address` \u2014 `@Size(1,255)` (if present)\n   - `addressLine1` \u2014 `@Size(1,255)`; `addressLine2` \u2014 `@Size(max 255)`\n   - `email` \u2014 `@Size(1,255)` + `@Email` (if present)\n\n## Inside `addOwner` (in execution order)\n\n3. **Idempotency short-circuit** \u2014 reads the `Idempotency-Key` header; if that key was already used and the owner it created still exists, returns that owner with **200 OK**, skipping everything below.\n4. **`validateRequiredOwnerFields`** \u2014 rejects blank (present-but-empty) `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`/`addressLine1`, `city`, `telephone` \u2192 `InvalidOwnerFieldsException` (400).\n5. **Map DTO \u2192 `Owner`** (`ownerMapper.toOwner`).\n6. **`normalizeTelephone`** *(validation + mutation)* \u2014 strips spaces/dashes/brackets, applies `+61` default & drops leading `0`, requires `+` followed by 8\u201315 digits, and enforces the exact national-number length per country code (`+61`\u21929, `+1`\u219210). Stores the E.164 value. Invalid \u2192 `InvalidOwnerFieldsException`.\n7. **`normalizeEmail`** *(validation + mutation)* \u2014 if present: must match the email pattern, is lower-cased/trimmed, and its domain must not be on the disposable-domain blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`). Stores the normalized value.\n8. **`applyAddress`** *(mutation)* \u2014 normalizes the flat or structured address (whitespace collapse, upper-case, street-abbreviation expansion) and composes the stored `address`.\n9. **`validatePostcode`** \u2014 if present: must be 4 digits, and must fall in the city's region range (Sydney/NSW 2000\u20132099, Melbourne/VIC 3000\u20133099, Brisbane/QLD 4000\u20134099); other cities accept any 4-digit code \u2192 `InvalidOwnerFieldsException`.\n10. **`rejectFutureRegistrationDate`** \u2014 supplied `registrationDate` may not be after today \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException`.\n11. **Default + `rollToBusinessDay`** *(mutation)* \u2014 defaults a missing date to today, then rolls forward off weekends and the fixed public-holiday list; stores the adjusted `registrationDate`.\n12. **`rejectDailyLimitReached`** \u2014 if \u2265 100 owners already share that registration date \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitExceededException`.\n13. **`rejectCityAtCapacity`** \u2014 if the city already holds \u2265 50 owners (case/whitespace-insensitive) \u2192 `OwnerCityCapacityExceededException`.\n14. **`setCapacityWarning`** *(mutation)* \u2014 `true` when the city holds 40\u201349 owners.\n15. **Compute `sharesHousehold`** flag from the DTO.\n16. **`setHouseholdId`** *(mutation)* \u2014 deterministic SHA-256-derived household id from region-V2 + last name + postcode.\n17. **`rejectDuplicateIdentity`** \u2014 unless `sharesHousehold`, rejects if the owner's identity key matches an existing non-deleted owner \u2192 `DuplicateOwnerIdentityException` (409).\n18. **`assignPossibleDuplicate`** *(mutation)* \u2014 sets `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf` for a soft match (same last-name Soundex + postcode, different identity key); skipped when `sharesHousehold`.\n19. **`setNamesakeCount`** *(mutation)* \u2014 count of existing owners with same first+last name.\n20. **`setBulkSignupWarning`** *(mutation)* \u2014 `true` when > 80 owners already share the registration date.\n21. **`setHouseholdSize`** *(mutation)* \u2014 count of household members, including this owner.\n22. **`setMembershipLevelCap`** *(mutation)* \u2014 one above the max membership level of existing household members (or null).\n23. **`setMemberId`** *(mutation)* \u2014 builds `<REGION><FY><HASH8><Luhn>`, de-duplicated with a `-n` suffix against existing member ids.\n\n## Side-effects after the owner is fully built\n\n24. **`clinicService.saveOwner(owner)`** \u2014 persists the owner (the DB write).\n25. **Idempotency record** \u2014 if a key was supplied, stores `key \u2192 owner.id` in the in-memory `idempotentOwnerIds` map.\n26. **Audit log line** \u2014 `AUDIT.info(\"Owner created: \u2026\")` (id, memberId, registrationDate, membershipLevel).\n27. **`emitOwnerCreatedEvent`** \u2014 increments the shared `OWNER_EVENT_SEQ` counter and emits the structured `OWNER_CREATED` JSON event to the `AUDIT` logger.\n28. **`enqueueWelcomeNotification`** \u2014 emits a welcome line to the `NOTIFY` logger.\n29. **Response** \u2014 maps to `OwnerDto`, sets the `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header, returns **201 CREATED**.\n\nA couple of things worth flagging: steps 3 and 25 give **idempotent** behavior only when callers pass an `Idempotency-Key`; and the duplicate/capacity/daily-limit checks (12, 13, 17) are read-then-write against `findAllOwners()` with no locking, so they are racy under concurrent creates."
